# Pull requests that moved shipped source and are cited in no changelog
# section, with the reason each one is excluded. Read by
# scripts/changelog-completeness.mjs.
#
# Format: <number>: <reason>, or <commit sha>: <reason> for a commit that
# reached `main` with no pull request. A sha key needs at least seven hex
# characters and at least one letter, which is what tells it from a number.
#
# A bare number is refused, and every entry that APPLIES to the release being
# checked is printed on a passing run too - an exclusion nobody can see is how
# a gate stops meaning anything.
#
# The first five are all from the 0.1.6 range. They are recorded here rather
# than written into a section that has already shipped, so that a run against
# that tag still reproduces green.
#
# From 0.1.7 on, the answer to a finding is an entry in the section. The one
# class that stays here is a merge that moves only a MEASUREMENT LEDGER or the
# machinery reading it: those files record what the pinned engines currently do,
# so a reader of the notes learns nothing from them and the rule they measure is
# written up under its own ruling. Anything that moves a clause, a corpus row or
# the oracle gets an entry.

